elevate-pam
===========

A Linux-PAM implementation in Rust. It has the same four stacks (auth,
account, session, password) and the same C pam_* ABI, so existing Linux-PAM
modules can load, and its modules are named and behave like the usual
pam_unix, pam_env, pam_limits and so on. The one big difference is that
service stacks are TOML files instead of /etc/pam.d text. The old format
can still be read when built with the legacy_pamd feature.

It is used by elevate, but nothing here depends on it.

It works for the stacks we use, but it is young. chauthtok in the builtin
pam_unix is not finished (it returns PAM_AUTHTOK_ERR), so be careful with
password-change stacks.

Layout
------

    crates/pam/              the engine, built as libelevate_pam
    crates/libpam-abi/       libpam.so.0-compatible shim
    crates/libpam-misc/      pam_misc helpers
    crates/elevate-pam-cli/  small CLI
    modules/                 loadable pam_*.so modules
    helpers/                 unix_chkpwd
    etc/                     example config and service stacks
    include/security/        C headers
    scripts/                 build and install

Most modules are also compiled into the library, so the .so files are
only needed if you would rather load them.

Building
--------

    make
    make test

Passwords are checked with elevate-crypto, which cargo pulls from git. To
build without it:

    cargo build --release -p elevate-pam --no-default-features \
      --features std,dynload,syslog,secure_mem,fail_delay,builtin_modules

The core also builds without std (make check-nostd).

Configuration
-------------

elevate-pam uses the first config it finds:

    $ELEVATE_PAM_CONFIG
    /etc/elevate-pam/elevate-pam.toml
    /etc/elevate-pam.toml
    ./elevate-pam.toml

Paths are set in its [paths] table, and what you leave out follows from
prefix. With no config file it uses the normal layout (/etc, /lib/security).
There is a commented example in etc/elevate-pam/elevate-pam.toml.

A service stack, services/other.toml:

    [service]
    name = "other"

    [[auth]]
    control = "required"
    module = "unix"

    [[account]]
    control = "required"
    module = "unix"

Installing
----------

    make install                     /lib, /etc, /bin
    make install DESTDIR=$PWD/pkg    stage it for a package
    make install PREFIX=/opt/pam     relocated

For a relocated install, set
ELEVATE_PAM_CONFIG=/opt/pam/etc/elevate-pam/elevate-pam.toml.

